{"kind":"request","text":"Give request custody one owner in the client, and let the command line install an application with no MCP service.\n\nFiled 2026-11-11 21:14 EST. Hugh asked for this work on 11 November and said to do it as soon as possible. Every fact below is read at main `df41e599`. My first advice was to park it until after the stable base, because it adds client exports and breaks none. Hugh's word replaces that advice. This request asks the planner to place it in the order `fc7576f8`, after the MCP boundary head that follows NF-1 (`6050f6ea`).\n\n## The problem\n\nA client that signs a request must keep the exact envelope before it sends it. After a lost reply, the client asks the scope to settle that envelope and never signs a second one. Three modules do this work on a device, with three formats.\n\n| Module | Size | Phases | Production consumer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `packages/client/src/request-custody.ts` (`Kept`, version 1) | 99 lines | `prepared`, `inflight`, `unknown`, `recorded`, `refused` | `browser-joining.ts` in the client |\n| `packages/client/src/request-attempts.ts` and `request-dispatch.ts` (`AttemptJournal`, version 2) | 171 lines | the same five | `apps/counter` only |\n| `packages/mcp/src/custody.ts`, with `sqlite-custody.ts` and the file store in `node.ts` | 518 and 315 lines, plus the file store | `prepared`, `sent`, `unknown`, `accepted`, `archived`, `refused`, `mismatch`, `settled` | MCP, and the command line through MCP |\n\n1. **The complete custody lives in the MCP package.** Only MCP's `Custody` keeps what travels beside an intent (detached texts, presented facts and values), preparation steps, a creation, a `resubmit` after a refusal, and an archived settlement. The client's `Kept` format states that it admits no grants, no detached texts and no presented facts.\n2. **Nothing in `custody.ts` is about MCP.** It imports the contract, the bytes package and `./metrics.ts`. Four calls to two metric functions are its whole tie to the package.\n3. **The names differ for one meaning.** The client says `inflight` and `recorded`. MCP says `sent` and `accepted`.\n4. **The command line installs through an MCP service.** `packages/cli/src/application-install-runtime.ts` builds an `McpService`, calls the tools `install_application` and `application_installation` by name, and reads `structuredContent[\"answer\"]`, `[\"item\"]`, `[\"state\"]` and `[\"phase\"]` by string key. `packages/cli/src/main.ts` takes its custody store from `@generalbusiness/dap-mcp/node`. The install logic is `#installApplication` at `packages/mcp/src/service.ts:1408`.\n5. **The client already holds the install parts that only MCP calls.** `signedApplicationInstall`, `signedApplicationInstall2`, `signedDeviceApplicationInstall`, `readApplicationInstallOptions` and `commonsInstallCheck` are client exports with MCP as their one production consumer.\n\nTwo things are not part of the problem. The originals of `packages/client/src/originals.ts` are copies that a membership scope keeps across devices. The page and MCP both use that one module, and it is the example to follow. `packages/scope` and `apps/views` import `@generalbusiness/dap-mcp` because they host the endpoint, its OAuth and its cards, and those imports are correct.\n\n## The work\n\nA design note comes first, then two heads.\n\n1. **Design note.** Decide the questions under \"Rulings\" below. State the one phase vocabulary, the store port, and what a browser store must do. One page is enough.\n2. **Head 1: custody moves.** Move `Custody`, `CustodyStore`, the record types, `decisive` and `memoryStore` to `packages/client`. Metrics become a port that the caller supplies. `packages/mcp` keeps the SQLite store, the file store and its own identity policy, and imports the rest. The stored bytes of a custody record do not change, because hosted agents and `ARTROOM_HOME/private/mcp-custody/` hold live records.\n3. **Head 2: install leaves the service.** Add a client function for the install request and one for the installation read. Each takes a handle, a custody and typed arguments, and returns a typed result. The MCP tools and the command line both call them. `application-install-runtime.ts` no longer builds an `McpService`. The command line keeps `@generalbusiness/dap-mcp` only for `dap mcp`.\n\n## Rulings the planner owes with the schedule\n\n- **Do `Kept` and `AttemptJournal` retire?** One option moves `browser-joining.ts` and Counter onto the moved custody with a browser store. The other keeps them as small formats and only aligns the phase names. Counter's journals in a browser carry wire version 2, and the cutover retires the old rooms.\n- **Which phase words win.** `sent` and `accepted` are in stored MCP records. `inflight` and `recorded` are in stored browser records.\n- **Where the store ports live.** A SQLite store and a file store are not MCP's by nature. They can move with custody or stay.\n\n## What to weigh\n\n- **Priority.** Hugh said as soon as possible. The order `fc7576f8` parks features. This work adds no feature: it moves an owner.\n- **Collision.** Both heads edit `packages/mcp/src/service.ts`. Order them after S4, after the cutover head, after NF-1 and after the MCP boundary head.\n- **Risk.** Custody is the guarantee that a request is never signed twice. The 518 lines move with their tests. A golden test over stored record bytes guards the move.\n- **Kernel.** No kernel file changes and no record form is added.\n- **Deployment.** The hosted MCP Workers carry head 1. `MCP_ENABLED` stays off until S4 lands.\n- **Later use.** One custody in the client is the store behind an \"awaited\" value: an intent, an item with states, a send, or created scopes, with a poll that returns pending or settled. MCP can render that value as a Task, the command line as `settle`, and a foldkit app as a Subscription. That type is not asked here.\n- **Size.** An estimate from reading, not a measurement: head 1 moves about 500 lines and changes few. Head 2 moves about 65 lines of `#installApplication` and removes 37 lines of the command line's runtime.","body":{"conditions":"A design note rules the phase words, the store port and whether Kept and AttemptJournal retire. Custody, CustodyStore, the record types and memoryStore live in packages/client, and packages/mcp imports them. The stored bytes of a custody record are unchanged, with a golden test. The command line installs an application and reads an installation with no McpService, through typed client functions that the MCP tools also call. npm run gate passes.","target_head":"df41e59964f09ce1d723ce870f5e4e5c6d8d4641","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}